# Creidyll Hoverboard - Core Safety Controller
# Author: Chief Architect
# 
# WARNING: This is the absolute bottom layer of the safety stack. 
# If this logic fails, the rider gets hurt. Do not optimize this for elegance. 
# Optimize it for predictability and deterministic failure.

# --- HARDWARE INTERFACE ---
# 16-bit ADC readings from the main sensor array. 
# We use 16-bit to preserve resolution for the analog pressure and temp sensors.
pin skirt_pressure input 16
pin battery_current input 16
pin battery_temp input 16
pin blower_rpm input 16

# Hardwired rider kill switch. Active low (0 = pressed).
pin emergency_button input 1

# Outputs to the power stage. 
# blower_pwm cuts thrust. main_contactor physically isolates the battery.
pin blower_pwm output 16
pin main_contactor output 1

# --- STATE DEFINITION ---
# Keep it simple. Complex state machines hide bugs. 
# We only need to know if we are safely on the ground, building pressure, 
# flying, or actively killing the thrust.
make a state_machine named flight_state with states GROUND, SPIN_UP, HOVER, EMERGENCY_DESCENT

# --- ABSOLUTE SAFETY OVERRIDES ---
# These are evaluated in pure combinational logic (always_comb). 
# They bypass the state machine and force a hard fault in <10ns. 
# No higher-level software or AI can override this.

# 1. Manual Kill: Rider pulled the plug. Drop immediately.
if emergency_button == 0 force flight_state to EMERGENCY_DESCENT

# 2. Loss of Lift: Cushion pressure dropped. 
# Threshold set to 1000 (approx 1000 Pa). Below this, the Coanda effect breaks down 
# and we risk a hard, unstable impact. Don't wait for the PID to figure it out.
if skirt_pressure < 1000 force flight_state to EMERGENCY_DESCENT

# 3. Electrical Fault: Battery is pulling too much current. 
# Indicates a short circuit, MOSFET failure, or severe motor stall.
if battery_current > 4000 force flight_state to EMERGENCY_DESCENT

# 4. Thermal Runaway: We saw cell degradation and swelling at 3200 in bench tests. 
# 3500 is the absolute hard kill line. Cut power before the pack vents.
if battery_temp > 3500 force flight_state to EMERGENCY_DESCENT

# 5. Mechanical Failure: Blower stalled, belt snapped, or impeller jammed. 
# No RPM means no lift, regardless of what the PWM is commanding.
if blower_rpm < 500 force flight_state to EMERGENCY_DESCENT

start machine
